meta {
  name: Create orders in bulk
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/bulk
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{partnerKey}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "items": [
      { "external_order_id": "BULK-{{$timestamp}}-1", "external_customer_id": "C-77", "amount": "250.00", "currency": "USD", "customer": { "email": "pat@example.com" } },
      { "external_order_id": "BULK-{{$timestamp}}-2", "external_customer_id": "C-78", "amount": "300.00", "currency": "USD", "customer": { "email": "sam@example.com" } }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  **Always 200, even when every item failed.** The status is about the batch request, which was
  understood; what happened to each order is in its own outcome. A 4xx would tell you to
  resubmit the whole batch including the orders that succeeded.

  Items come back in the order you sent them, each with a verdict. Isolation is the promise:
  one item failing does not affect its neighbours.

  `BATCH_DEADLINE_EXCEEDED` is retryable and applies per item — anything not *started* before
  the deadline comes back with it, while items already running are allowed to finish.
}
